# Link & Parameter Discovery Rule (TBHM v4 & 40-Check Multi-Agent Framework)

When tasked with web crawling, parameter mining, client-side JS analysis, or uncovering hidden inputs:

1. Follow the **40-Check Audit Matrix** defined in `.agents/skills/linkparamdiscovery/references/checklist_40_tracker.md`.
2. Divide tasks across the 5 specialized subagents:
   - **Subagent 01 (Crawlers & Linked Discovery):** `.agents/skills/linkparamdiscovery/subagents/subagent_01_crawlers_linked_discovery.md`
   - **Subagent 02 (JS Mining & Source Maps):** `.agents/skills/linkparamdiscovery/subagents/subagent_02_js_mining_sourcemaps.md`
   - **Subagent 03 (Parameter Mining & Forms):** `.agents/skills/linkparamdiscovery/subagents/subagent_03_parameter_mining_forms.md`
   - **Subagent 04 (Real-time, WS & Event Handlers):** `.agents/skills/linkparamdiscovery/subagents/subagent_04_realtime_websockets_events.md`
   - **Subagent 05 (API Formats, SSO & Workflows):** `.agents/skills/linkparamdiscovery/subagents/subagent_05_api_formats_workflows.md`
3. Incorporate `wordlists/params.txt` for all parameter brute-forcing.
4. Save structured outputs in `artifacts/discovered_parameters.json` and mark items complete in `checklist_40_tracker.md`.
